WEBVTT

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.570
How do we climb this?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.570
Leave it to me. I have the perfect route.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.530
Shall we see where he takes us?

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.700
We'll stay and watch the bus.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.720
Have fun!

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.250
Thank you.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.670
What is this place?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:50.770
From here, we'll take the ropeway. 
Please board... board... board...

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.500
Searching. Searching.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.860
This again?

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.140
Maybe we can go across this.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.000
Serval-chan!

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.560
What now? Boss isn't saying anything.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.820
Want to try and climb the cliff? 
Looks like we could go up from over there.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.470
I don't think I can do that.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:33.430
I am Crested Ibis.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:38.360
I am searching for friends.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.260
Where are you, friends?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:51.330
My friends, I am searching for you.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:54.510
Oh, friends...

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.070
That voice sure was something.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:04.770
Yeah, it really was.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.500
Good afternoon.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:13.230
Order: Pelecaniformes
Family: Threskiornithidae
Genus: Nipponia

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.900
It's nice to meet you. I am Crested Ibis.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.690
How was my song?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.080
Very, um, p-powerful.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.360
And the way you fluffed your feathers... 
It was very beautiful.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.410
Thank you. It's so nice to have an audience.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.290
Well, I'm glad you two look happy.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.630
Does that mean you want an encore?

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.440
Huh?!

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.950
I am Crested Ibis!

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.980
M-Maybe later!

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.970
I am searching for friends!

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.970
Take it easy, okay?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.440
What were you doing here?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.690
We need to get to the top of the mountains.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:19.230
Boss said that there was 
an easy way up from here.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.300
Would you like me to carry you?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.410
I was going to fly over 
these mountains anyway.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.060
Really? You can do that?

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.730
I could carry one of you. Probably.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.780
Boss won't talk to anyone but you,
Kaban-chan. He's all yours.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.260
Are you sure about this? 
Maybe you should wait...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.080
I'm fine. It's at the top 
of the mountain, right?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.760
Let's race to see who gets up there first!

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.050
Time for us to take off, too.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.650
This is incredible. We're flying!

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.040
First time in the sky?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:18.580
Yes!

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.150
I'm not too heavy for you?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.090
I'm fine.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.720
I used to have big wings,

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.660
but I can fly more easily with these wings 
than when I was a regular animal.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:43.430
The crested ibis is a large bird with 
a wingspan of 140 centimeters.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:48.940
Its body is white, with a deep pink color 
on the undersides of its wings.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:53.910
In Japanese, this beautiful shade of red (<i>toki</i>) 
is even named after the crested ibis (<i>toki</i>).

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:57.500
You know so much about me.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.340
Oh, it's not me, it's Lucky-san.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.050
Could you be a fan of mine?

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.080
Your fan?

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:10.640
Oh, yes, I think you're incredible.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:17.070
My dear fan... I'll be careful 
not to drop you.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.490
I appreciate it. Thank you.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.500
The call of the crested ibis is 
throaty, like that of the crow,

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.690
and said to be very annoying.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.070
Th-That wasn't me. I...

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.660
I love your singing!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.700
Really? You're making me blush.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.150
Yes, really. It's so loud, I bet 
it can be heard from far away.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.880
Their call is also said to be nasal.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:51.430
Many folk tales were written 
with this as a theme.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:59.080
Th-That wasn't me, I swear!

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:03.940
Lucky-san, I get it. You can stop now!

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.950
Did you say you came from the savanna?

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.820
It's so hot there. I can't believe 
you came through it.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.330
It was hot, yes.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.100
Where did you come from, Crested Ibis-san?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.130
I flew over that forest.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.470
I don't like places that are too hot or too cold.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.400
It's amazing how the 
temperature and humidity

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.790
are so different when these areas 
are right next to each other.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.360
Due to the Sandstar, the temperature,

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:50.190
humidity, and even sunlight have changed.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.760
Sandstar is a mysterious substance.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.950
There is still so much that 
even we do not know about it.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.030
Sandstar...

00:07:58.030 --> 00:07:59.940
It comes from over there.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.650
You said you were born 
from this year's eruption?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:08.340
It seems that way.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.250
I hope you find out what 
kind of animal you are.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.470
This is tougher than I thought.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.580
That was a close one.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.320
I hope Kaban-chan and Crested Ibis are okay.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:34.410
Hold on, Kaban-chan! I'll be there soon!

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:45.900
Food tastes extra delicious up here, 
doesn't it? It's a new discovery.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.420
Isn't that the truth?

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.500
<i>I'll have to tell Serval-chan about it later.</i>

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.170
Maybe I should make a Japari bun song.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.550
"Poles and Japari Buns."

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:05.110
Japari buns eaten at the top 
of poles are so delicious...

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.750
Now, let's go...

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.730
You really love singing, don't you?

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:16.610
It feels a little different as a Friend, though.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:20.490
I wonder if there's a different 
way to sing in this body...

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.330
I know. You try singing.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.710
Huh?!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:29.760
You seem to know a lot about singing, 
and you knew a lot about me, too.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.030
No, that was Lucky-san.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.240
Come on.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.720
Uh...

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:36.340
Like this.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:44.350
Japari buns eaten at the top 
of poles are so delicious...

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:54.190
Japari buns eaten at the top of poles 
are more delicious than usual...

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.310
A new discovery!

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.500
I knew it. You're very good.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.310
Did you do something special?

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.510
The way you breathe, maybe?

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:10.420
Uh, I'm not sure. It's best to breathe 
from your diaphragm... I think.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.910
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:16.150
But the cold might be harsh on your throat.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:20.140
I see. So maybe where you 
sing makes a difference.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.310
You're eager to learn, aren't you?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:31.700
The Japanese crested ibis has a long, 
curved black beak with a red tip.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:54.190
Sado City Toki Forest Park, Higuchi-oneesan (Ishikawa Prefecture)

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:37.360
Their faces are red and have no feathers.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.440
Their legs are red, as well.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:43.200
Their feathers are normally white,

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.360
with a beautiful pale 
pink-orange color mixed in.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:50.510
Unlike mandarin duck pairs and so on,

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:53.900
it's said that they basically mate for life.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.090
Alpacas are known for their 
very soft, voluminous fleece.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:11:24.180
Nasu Alpaca Farm, Abeo-neesan (Tochigi Prefecture)

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:01.570
They're covered in so much fine fleece

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:04.430
that you can't imagine the 
shape of their body beneath.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.810
They're endearing animals.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:11.900
They have very cute mouths. 
The upper lip is split, like a rabbit's,

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.080
so they look cute when they eat.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.460
They live in herds and,

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:19.120
like with monkeys, one alpaca leads the herd,

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:24.450
but in their social structure, everyone 
doesn't have to listen to the alpha male.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.850
This place is breathtaking.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.530
Is that it?

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.750
Hi there!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:16.300
Welcome to Japari Café. Come on in.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.250
Make yourselves at home!

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.730
Um, okay.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.470
Gosh, I've been waiting so long. 
Finally, some customers!

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.300
I'm so happy!

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:28.510
So, what'll you have? 
We have lots to choose from.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:35.400
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Camelidae 
Genus: Vicugna

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:32.450
This is called "black tea." 
The professor taught me that!

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:35.400
Hot water comes out of here, 
so you use that, and...

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.400
Excuse me, but we're looking for 
a place to charge our battery.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.150
So you're not customers? Ptoo!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.200
I'm so sorry!

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:47.200
This is the battery.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:51.200
Oh, in that case, maybe...

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.400
Is this what you're looking for?

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.710
Is it?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.010
This is it. This is it.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.230
What is this thing?

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:09.100
Amazing, right? Thanks to this,
we can make tea.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:12.240
Did you make this, Alpaca-san?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.390
No way. It was here from the beginning.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:19.290
Though I don't know what it is, either.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.650
That will do. Please wait for about an hour.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.980
Huh? Did it get darker in here?

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:27.280
Oh, that...

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.660
I want to drink this "black tea."

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:34.290
Actually, when you disconnect that cable 
I showed you, the hot water won't work.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:37.300
I'm sorry. Is that okay?

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:41.480
No problem. It's not like 
I get any customers.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.170
When the "charging" thingy 
is done, I'll make you a cup.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.670
Do you really get so few customers?

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:50.410
That's right. No one comes here.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.870
But it's such a lovely place.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.180
Maybe no one knows about it.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:14:00.700
I told a lot of Friends at the bottom of 
the mountain about it, but no one comes.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:04.290
Maybe they don't know where it is?

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.930
I only heard about it from her.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:09.780
Huh? Is it that hard to find?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.590
There are so many mountains here. 
You pass right by it.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:18.530
Really? I just climb up,
 so I'd never considered that.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:20.670
I think only those who 
can fly would go this way.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:25.090
Huh? But it's a piece of cake, 
even if you're carrying things.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:29.090
Um, I know of something we could try.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.180
Do you mind if we pull up the grass here?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:41.690
Not at all. Weeding is a lot of work, 
so I'd appreciate the help.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:46.230
Could you pull it for me where I direct you to?

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:49.620
First, we'll go straight in that direction.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.070
You got it.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:51.070
Roger.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:55.490
Pull, pull...

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.560
Makes me want to sing.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:00.890
Can you keep curving slowly in that direction?

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:04.290
Weeding. Weeding. Weeding.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:12.930
Alpaca, what made you decide 
to start a café here?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:17.260
Folks go through here to get to the 
next Area all the time, right?

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:18.520
The bird types do, yes.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.810
So I thought it would be the 
perfect place to take a rest.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:27.330
Then, one day, I found this little building 
on the next mountain over.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:31.290
I heard that when tea is served at a 
place like this, it's called a "café."

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:34.030
So I had them teach me how 
to make it at the library.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:38.490
I thought all I needed next 
was to have everyone come,

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:41.590
but nobody comes by at all.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.140
May I stop weeding for the moment?

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.170
Okay.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:48.640
What got into him?

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:49.450
Dunno.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:53.820
Okay!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.400
Can you fly up for me?

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.130
Huh? Sure thing.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.730
I wonder why she wants us to fly.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:02.440
Wow, I'm flying!

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.080
Look below us.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.570
If everyone sees this, they won't pass it by.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:21.200
Amazing, amazing! 
Now they'll notice my café!

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.310
That's great.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.140
Huh?

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.400
Serval-chan!

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.340
Are you okay?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.730
I had no idea climbing mountains 
would be this hard.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:38.600
Oh, gosh! A customer already?

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:42.870
Don't push yourself, okay?

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.350
I got a bit carried away!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.440
You could have just waited.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.440
Good work. Here you go.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.780
Drink up, drink up.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.660
You seem excited, Alpaca-san.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.590
You bet I am!

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.370
So this is a café!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.740
And this is "tea"...

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:04.520
Thanks for the tea.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.420
Cafés are great.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.690
They're relaxing.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.470
I hope everyone notices it.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.720
I think it's time for a song.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:33.510
My name is Crested Ibis.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:37.240
I am searching for friends.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:44.120
Where are you, my friends?

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.220
Oh, friends!

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:54.300
What happened? Your voice 
is way better than before.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.420
It's true. It was easier to sing than usual.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:01.150
Earlier, you said you were going to sing,

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.530
so I made tea that would 
be good for your throat.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.310
You feel nice and warm inside, right?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.890
I think I'll be a regular customer.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.020
Awesome!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.670
One more cup... No, lots more, please.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.110
You can drink lots, but it'll still taste the same.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.970
Amazing! What is it, what is it?

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.290
I never knew you could use it like this.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:31.300
It seems that this can carry you 
to the bottom of the mountain.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.450
Wow, wow!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.570
I wanna try! I wanna try!

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:42.350
Take care, then. 
I hope your bus thingy works.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.850
Thank you.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.640
When you want to hear me sing, 
you can call for me anytime.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.650
Yup! Stay well, Crested Ibis!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.710
Stop by again, okay?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:19:03.180
Pedal, pedal...

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.280
We will!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.590
That was a wonderful café, wasn't it?

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.020
Let's go back for more sometime.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:05.450
Yeah.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.410
Shall I make another cup?

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:13.130
You bet.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:20.630
Order: Pelecaniformes
Family: Threskiornithidae
Genus: Eudocimus

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.490
What's happening here?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:22.670
I saw this strange shape on the ground, 
and then I heard singing.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.350
Pedal, pedal...

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.410
My legs feel like jelly.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.150
Good work.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.900
Welcome back!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.400
Thanks.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.420
So, any luck?

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.570
I think it worked. Here it is.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:01.570
We did it!

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:05.130
So how does the bus thingy move?

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:06.330
I don't know.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.250
Wouldn't it, like, kick its feet?

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:11.350
Which parts are its feet?

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.640
Awesome!

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.540
Wait, wait!

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.670
Let me on, let me on, let me on!

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.830
Stop! Move!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.170
Be careful!

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:36.340
Thank you for your help.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.450
See you again!

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.450
You all be careful.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:38.880
See ya!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.290
Bye-bye!

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.620
Bye-bye!

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.490
This bus thing is incredible.

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:51.020
Yup, it sure is.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:54.840
Serval-chan, you can see 
the mountain from before.

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:59.980
It's so big. No wonder it was a tough climb.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:04.500
Serval-chan, I really don't think 
you're supposed to go up it on foot.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.460
That reminds me. Listen to this!

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:09.300
On the way up, I thought I saw a 
place where I could climb trees,

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:13.180
but it peeled off, and I fell all 
the way down to the bottom.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:15.320
What?! Were you okay?

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:52.300
Who's there?

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:58.220
That startled me.

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:02.560
Are you all right? Do you want 
to drink some water?

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:07.070
E-Excuse me, have you seen someone 
wearing something like this?

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:13.110
Oh, yes, she passed through here. 
What about her?

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:18.880
Oh, so this really was the right way. 
Way to go, Raccoon-san.

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:21.260
I must catch her quickly!

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:23.630
That... That....

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:28.740
Thanks, lady!

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:34.200
There are Ceruleans out. 
You girls be careful!

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:37.320
PPP Preview!

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:39.410
This week, let's learn about the Tsuchinoko.

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:42.090
Apparently the Tsuchinoko snores.

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:43.390
Snores?

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:44.530
What would that sound like?

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.690
Is that snoring?

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:47.690
Is that supposed to be snoring?

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:48.850
Oh, that was sniffing.

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:50.030
You were sniffing?

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:50.970
That was sniffing.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:52.000
I can't tell!

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:53.260
Wrong noise!

00:23:52.670 --> 00:23:54.080
I couldn't tell at all!

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:54.200
That's not snoring!

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:56.750
Next time, "Desert Area."
